"either"
"The coin is about an inch and a half in diameter, and about an eighth of an

inch thick and comprised of solid gold.  On the @eface@n of the coin is the

picture of a legendary lord, and on the @ereverse@n is a stunning portrait of

the forests of the Vaasa.

"
E
"face heads front"
"The years of built-up tarnish have made this gold coin appear to be

bronze.  The coin appears to be in fair condition, and most of the fine

details are still visible through the wearing of the years.  The face of

Lord Richard of Medienne has been molded into the front of the coin,

though the image must be many years old by now.  His features are strong

and youthful, and his expression is one of determination against many

difficult trials that lay before him. Above his profile is the date of

birth, while the lower portion of the coin remains blank.

"
E
"back tails reverse"
"The edges of the coin are traced by a highly detailed trio of interwoven

bands that have each been etched with their own individual patterns of

fine, complex celtic knots.  Inside the ornate frame is an equally

detailed landscape scene depicting the mighty shuvana trees of the Vaasa

standing at the foot of a series of cliffs.  Atop one of the cliffs,

there rises a tall stone spire that stretches high into the sky to a

point where only the heavens stand taller.

"
