"either"
"The coin is about an inch and a half in diameter, and about an eighth of an

inch thick and comprised of solid copper.  On the @eface@n of the coin is the

picture of a legendary saint, and on the @ereverse@n is a stunning portrait of

the Sea of Stars.

"
E
"face heads front"
"Although tarnished from the great number of years of use, the profile of

the patron saint Serinblum XVII is still recognizable on the face of

this copper coin.  His sharp features seem somewhat haggard, though it

is impossible to tell whether or not it was originally part of the coin,

or if the countless hands that have handled this coin have worn away its

shape with their hands.  Around the edge of the coin are enscribed the

dates of Saint Serinblum XVII's birth and death.

"
E
"back tails reverse"
"The intricate designs once etched into this coin have been worn away

over the many years since it was minted, however the larger patterns

have remained in fair condition.  A trio of ropes woven around each

other encircles the center of the coin, which contains an image of the

Sea of Stars, as seen from the Cairn Mountains.  The sun has just begun

to peek over the horizon, and its rays illuminate the surface of the

water beneath it.  Despite the rough aging of the coin's condition, the

skill and vision of the artist are still very evident.

"
P
