gleaming blades or axes, the magi glare from black or red hoods and clutch

wooden staves, the priests' garb is so lifelike that it looks like real cloth,

and the rogues' impish smiles make them seem ready to leap from the card and

rob you blind if you look away for too long.  The non-face cards are somewhat

more plain, but the numbers and suits still painted with a steady hand.  Two

nearly flat strips of cloth have been used to wrap around the cards and keep

them from spilling about when being carried around.  On the back of the top

card is scrawled, barely legible, \"help cards\".

"
