"either"
"Snowy-white griffon feathers have been neatly sewn to a sturdy white leather

jerkin.  Done in an overlapping, scale-like design, the pattern of feathers

descends from the neck of the garment to the hem of the sleeves and waist. 

Upon closer inspection, very fine emerald dust is detectable on the tips of

each feather which gives a sharp edge to the otherwise ordinary decoration. 

The short sleeves of the soft jerkin end at the person's elbows, lending to a

habit of wearing a thinner type of shirt underneath for added style, as well

as protection and warmth.  A long slit has been made in the collar of the

jerkin which runs straight down the front of the garment to nearly the center

of the fabric, thus allowing for a looser fit and more freedom of movement for

the individual.  Placed as eyelets which run along the edges of the slit,

beautiful, pearlescent opals having holes cut in their middles keep an

intricately braided silk string of emerald and silver from tearing at the

soft, white leather of the jerkin.  At the tips of this magnificent,

ornamental silk braid, two small emeralds have been tied so the threading of

the string does not become undone.

"
P
