"either"
"Long and powerful looking but seriously flawed by several cracks in it, the

horn still retains the memory of its original grace.  The horn is just a touch

over two feet long and perhaps eight inches wide at its base.  It has the

consistency of ivory but the color of dark, stained oak with natural red hues

to it.  The horn has a reflective sheen and looking into it you seems to peer

through the surface in much the same way you would when looking at a tigreseye

stone.  If not for the cracks nearly splitting it apart in places it would be

an incredible momento.

"
