plates of some very thin, granite-hard metal have been riveted onto the

leather backing on the chest, back, and shoulders.  The inside of the leather

is lined with a quilted silken undergarment, presumably to protect against

bruising and scratches from the rivets.  Ordinarily armors of this type are

not light or flexible enough to be the preferred choice for those who would

sneak in the night, but this armor is a perfect compromise between excellent

protection, flexibility, and weight.

