"either"
"Underneath a solid sheet of diamond lies an ornate sundial easily twenty feet

in diameter, carved from a strange, polished white stone.  The sundial has two

rings: A fixed outer ring for telling time via the sun, and a free-spinning

inner ring for time by moonlight.  The inner ring is aligned with the markings

pointing to the current phase of the moon, as identified by an iridescent

replica of the actual moon set into a circular opening within the central

disk.  Strangely enough, where the gnomon should have been to cast its shadow

lies a carved golden symbol of the scales of justice.  By some manner of

magic, it appears to be casting a perfect shadow across the surface of the

sundial.


"
