E
"either"
"@ROVERVIEW@n


The general concept of Val'Abun is that at one point, the city was connected to

the main world via a permanent gate fashioned by powerful wizards.  The forces

within the gate were such that only the more powerful could make the journey

alive.  At one point treachery came into play (of what sort is yet undecided)

and the gate was destroyed, effectively cutting off the two worlds.  Currently

we are thinking of using the broken obelisk as the site of the old gate.


@RDENIZENS@n


Every creature imaginable is found here both humanoid and otherwise, including

those you wouldn't normally see together.  It is the law that there is to be no

violence or theft on public grounds, so do not be surprised when you see evil

undead creatures existing unmolested in the presence of those of a holy order.

They are free to avoid and dislike each other, but any violent action will be

met with severe punishment.


@RSTRUCTURE@n


The city is divided into five sections:


1. @CThe Government District@n


Contains an administrative building, jail-house, and the Val'Abun academy.  It

is where people will end up when they first enter the town, and will serve

mainly as a way to acquaint players with the new city, and provide trainers for

various skills.


2. @CThe Bazaar@n


The lifeblood of Val'Abun, the bazaar is a giant marketplace.  Roughly circular

in design, it is split into two concentric rings with shops at every corner.

At the heart of the bazaar lies the @Wscales of justice@n, an ancient, sentient

artifact which can see into the soul and mind of beings.  When awoken to

perform its function, the scales examine the accused and acts as both judge and

jury.  Those found guilty are punished on the spot by the artifact in the form

of a crippling mind attack (exp drain: currently thinking of player_level^4 as

the penalty), and are summarily expelled from the city for a short period of

time.


3. @CThe Cobalt Faction@n


The denizens of the city are split into three factions, each with their

separate area of the town.  The @bcobalt@n faction is guided by law, and they

have a very orderly and structured grounds (think new york).  They are home to

both creatures of good and evil.  In fact, it is rumored that the leader of the

cobalt faction is an evil liche.


4. @CThe Crimson Faction@n


The @rcrimson@n faction is ruled by chaos, and this is reflected in the

sprawled and confusing nature of their area of the city (think boston).  They

are constantly at odds with the cobalt faction.


5. @CThe Emerald Faction@n


The @gemerald faction@n champions neutrality, and thus finds itself at odds

with both the cobalt and crimson factions.  They are seen as an annoyance by

the others as they often try to meddle in the affairs of both in hopes of

achieving a relative balance between law and chaos.


@RNOTES ON THE FACTIONS@n


At this point, the areas for each of the factions are purely at the conceptual

stage and lack even so much as a general structure.  We were hoping to have

each of the areas designed such that each would have their own private shops,

customs, runnable mobs, and quests.  As far as restrictions for gaining access

to each area, we haven't really decided on the details.  This is something that

I feel could use some group brain-storming.


@RTHE UNVEILING@n


We were planning on creating a sort of \"world quest\" to reopen the gate.  In

terms of traveling through the newly opened gate, it was going to be set to

allow high level non-remorts, and any-level remorts through.  The concept there

being that old souls are more powerful, and thus able to survive passage.  We

are also considering creating a quest to acquire an item that will allow them

safe passage (still within level/remort requirements), to make it a bit more

difficult to gain entry.  The person/group performing the world quest would be

given this item at the completion, all others would need to complete the side

quest.


@RMISCELLANEOUS@n


Mention was made earlier of a jail-house, and of the scales of justice as a tool

of law enforcement.  The city is protected by a troop of flying, grouped

sorcerers, which will come to the aid of those in the public areas (Government

District

they will immediately stop the combat (peace command), and imprison the

attackers in the jail-house.  After a short while in captivity, they will be

brought before the scales of justice by the Val'Abun justice officiator and

judged on the spot.


What this means is that it is still possible to get away with theft/murder in

Val'Abun, if you are fast enough.  The city/mobs are going to be designed with

this in mind, and we plan on putting equipment on some of the mobs in these

\"protected\" areas (ala the Darkhaven Bank Guard) to facilitate seeing the law

in action.  In other words, nobody will risk the penalty of the scales of

justice unless there is a good reason to do so.  Merchants of course will still

be safe rooms to prevent abuse, but there will be some other mobs which will be

assailable for fun and profit.


If anybody has any questions/comments on all of this, give me (Semix) a holler.


@RNOTE@n: Incase you forget, Val'Abun is located at #28500.

"
P
