"Only vaguely humanoid, a corpse lies crumpled here against the stone pillar in

the center of the study.  The flesh has withered away with the absence of

moisture, now pressed against unfamiliar bones.  Instead of four appendages,

this creature possesses six, and a squat, rotund body like that of some sort

of sickly, monstrous tick.  Each appendage ends in a grasping claw, frozen

forever in rigor.  Any clothing that it might have once been wearing has long

since disintigrated, although whether from time or the acidic atmosphere is

uncertain.  Almost thankfully, the skull of the corpse is missing, making it

impossible to see how alien this creature might have been when alive.


One hand of the creature still clutches an intact book, which lies open to the

first page.

