color and the texture of oily leather.  A series of hammered metal has been

pressed into the front cover of the book.  The hide covering almost completely

conceals all four edges of the paper, only allowing a glimpse at the yellowed

parchment inside.  Three hide bands keep the codex shut, each with a single

black symbol of hammered metal pressed into it.  It takes no great insight or

detection ability to determine that this book is magical - it nearly thrums

with magical energy.

