"A golden-colored sword with parallel sides, swords of this type are ordinarily

designed to be a stabbing weapon; this fancy ceremonial gladius was obviously

never meant to be used in actual combat.  The hilt of the sword is a dense

hardwood, gilted with a thin foil.  Ancient writing encircles the waisted

hilt, faint silver lettering in a language that resembles, but is clearly not,

humanic.  The bladed edges and point are dull, but the blade is still

brilliantly weighted and could probably be used if the wielder were desperate.

"
