"read"
"@I@I@I@I@I@I@I@I@I@I@eOn Probability and Paradox@n

@I@I@I@I@I@I@I@I(A Treatise on the Nature of Temporal Magic)


Introduction.


The discipline of probability has fundamentally changed the way we do magic

and the method by which we devise our spells.  Many scholars have argued that

it is by luck alone that we have not, in our ignorance, torn the universe

assunder with our careless use of magical energy.  Indeed, the study of

probability when applied to magical constructs has affected a revolution in

the mage community, and has ushered in an era of responsible spell casting

previously unknown within our ranks.


Yet, despite the rapid infiltration of responsibility and calls for greater

care within the confines of our individual laboratories, my esteemed

colleagues forget that magic has been worked in this realm - and many others,

both within and beyond our means to access - for countless millenia.  This

new-found paradigm, which I shall call here conscientious casting, is all well

and good, and I am certainly an advocate for saftey in our mutual work.

However, I believe that it is unnecessary and, dare I say, detrimental to

approach our profession with what borders on cowardice.

"
